   190	> **COROLLARY SK-2'.** *Every row with `g = 2` and `n | d` — i.e. `(d,n) = (2u, 2)`, all
   191	> `u >= 2` — is dead.* Indeed `c = Pi_1` is a product of two transpositions: `c = 1` is
   192	> Lemma SK-2; `c` a `3`-cycle confines every entry to the three letters of its support, giving
   193	> `im <= S_3`; `c` a double transposition forces every block to be its two disjoint factors,
   194	> giving `im <= V_4`.
   195	
   196	This generalises the promoted `(4,2)` closure to the whole `n = 2` column at once, by a
   197	shorter argument than the `(4,2)` exponent-sum computation.
   198	
   199	### 2.3 THEOREM SK-1: the family is removable from the cage, at every degree
   200	
   201	> **THEOREM SK-1 (uniform kill of the `(u,1)` family).** *Let `D` be an escaping `N = 4`
   202	> residual branch curve. Put `d_min := min { deg T(D) : T in Aut(A^2) }`, the minimum being
   203	> over projective degrees of the images. Then `d_min` is attained, and in any attaining gauge
   204	> the degree pair `(d,n)` satisfies `n` does not divide `d`. Consequently the reduced shape of
   205	> `D` in that gauge is `(odd u, 2)` or `(4,3)`, never `(u,1)`.*
   206	
   207	*Proof.* The set `{deg T(D)}` is a nonempty set of positive integers, so the minimum is
   208	attained; fix an attaining `T_0` and write `D_0 = T_0(D)`. By promoted target-automorphism
   209	invariance `D_0` is again a residual branch curve carrying the forbidden representation, and it
   210	has a birational polynomial parametrisation `(P,Q)`. If `deg P = deg Q` compose with the linear
   570	   column at `g = 2`, and Lemma SK-3 kills every `n = 2` row by (M-INF) — three disjoint
   571	   confirmations.
   572	2. **Family `(odd u, 2)`.** Outer fixedness is exactly the deformed braid relation
   573	   `X W^m X = W^{m+1}` (3.1). At `g = 2` this is solved completely: the row is dead unless
   574	   `u = 3 (mod 6)` (Theorem SK-4), which deletes `(10,4), (14,4), (22,4), (26,4), ...` at a
   575	   stroke; the survivors are `d = 6, 18, 30, 42, ...` and `d = 6` is separately dead by the
   576	   promoted explicit-family ROW-KILL. For every `g = 2` survivor `Pi in V_4`, so the
   577	   `S_3`-resolvent descends automatically — the descent half of the `(6,4)` chain is
   578	   degree-free and available. The classification half is not: the consumed input is literally
   579	   a *degree-6* theorem. `OPEN[SHAPE-2-INNER-g>=3]`, `OPEN[SHAPE-2-INFINITY-Z3]`.
   580	3. **Family `(4,3)`, i.e. `(4g, 3g)` — NOT killed.** Outer fixedness is (4.1). Theorem SK-5
   581	   holds at every `g`: outside the constant stratum `Pi` is a `3`-cycle, so the `S_3`-resolvent
   582	   never descends and the NO-TORUS/Shirane route is structurally unavailable — a permanent
   583	   redirection, not a gap. At `g = 2` the constant stratum is dead and the non-constant stratum
   584	   is a single explicit `phi`-orbit; `(8,6)` survives, as the promoted ledger already has it.
   585	   `OPEN[SHAPE-3-ALL-g]`.
   586	4. **Net effect on the campaign-pin residual.** The "unconditional layer" of
   587	   `campaign-pin-gpt55-20260901.md:220-240` shrinks as follows. The `(u,1)` line is **deleted**.
   588	   The `(odd u,2)` line is cut to `u = 3 (mod 6)` at `g = 2` and is untouched for `g >= 3`. The
   589	   `(4,3)` line is untouched. Concretely, of the twenty pairs listed there for
   590	   `d in {10,12,14,15,16}`, **thirteen are deleted by SK-1 and two more — `(10,4)` and
   591	   `(14,4)` — by SK-4**, leaving five:
   592	
   593	   ```text
   594	   d=10:  none
   595	   d=12:  (12,8)  [g=4, shape (3,2)] ,  (12,9)  [g=3, shape (4,3)]
   596	   d=14:  none
   597	   d=15:  (15,6)  [g=3, shape (5,2)] ,  (15,10) [g=5, shape (3,2)]
   598	   d=16:  (16,12) [g=4, shape (4,3)]
   599	   d=18:  (18,4)  [g=2, shape (9,2)] ,  (18,12) [g=6, shape (3,2)]
   600	   ```
   601	
   602	   and the same two rules applied at every degree. `(18,4)` is the first genuinely new
   603	   `g = 2` survivor beyond `(6,4)`.
   604	5. **Where the remaining effort should go.** Every surviving stratum has the same shape of
   605	   residual: the outer level is satisfiable, so the kill must come from the inner braid `iota`,
   606	   whose exponent sum is pinned by (1.1)/(4.2) but whose individual block exponents are not.
   607	   The `(4,2)` closure worked because `e(iota) = 1` on two parameters. Two concrete successors,
   608	   in priority order: `OPEN[TRIPLE-COVER-TSCHIRNHAUS-SPLIT]` (a positive answer gives `6 | d`
   609	   and kills every family-2 and family-3 row with `6` not dividing `d`, including `(8,6)` — but
   610	   by SK-5 only via the constant stratum in family 3), and `OPEN[SHAPE-2-INFINITY-Z3]`, made
   611	   sharp by (3.4): all affine nodes contribute `A_1` points with local `pi_1 = Z/2` and hence
   612	   no `Z/3`, so the entire `Z/3`-obstruction sits at one point over the place at infinity.
   613	
   614	## 6. Typed verdict table
   615	
   616	| Family | Scope | Verdict | Instrument |
   617	|---|---|---|---|
   618	| `(u,1)`, all `u >= 2`, all `g >= 2` | every degree | **KILLED** | SK-1 (minimal-gauge descent + Chau re-run) |
   619	| `(u,1)`, `g = 2` | every `u` | **KILLED** (independent) | SK-2' |
   620	| any row with `n = 2` | every `d` | **KILLED** (independent) | SK-3 ((M-INF), `n <= p(a)`) |
   621	| proposed collapse rerun `\|im\| <= 6` at `n'=1` | all `(ug,g)` | **REFUTED** | SK-0; promoted `(6,2)` tuple |
   622	| `(odd u,2)`, `g = 2`, `u != 3 (mod 6)` | `d = 10,14,22,26,...` | **KILLED** | SK-4 |
   623	| `(odd u,2)`, `g = 2`, `u = 3 (mod 6)`, `u >= 9` | `d = 18,30,42,...` | **OPEN** | outer battery satisfied; `Pi in V_4` |
   624	| `(odd u,2)`, `g >= 3` | all | **OPEN** | `OPEN[SHAPE-2-INNER-g>=3]` |
   625	| `(4,3)`, `g = 2`, constant stratum | `(8,6)` | **KILLED** | SK-2 + realisability |
   626	| `(4,3)`, `g = 2`, non-constant | `(8,6)` | **OPEN** | single explicit `phi`-orbit |
   627	| `(4,3)`, `g >= 3` | all | **OPEN** | `OPEN[SHAPE-3-ALL-g]` |
   628	| `S_3`/Shirane route in family 3 | every `g` | **CLOSED NEGATIVE** | SK-5 (`Pi` a `3`-cycle) |
   629	| degree-free classification input for family 2 | — | **NOT FOUND** | Shirane is a degree-6 theorem |
   630	| `6 \| deg B` Cardano divisibility | — | **CONDITIONAL** | needs split Tschirnhaus bundle; typed OPEN |
