   200	## 5. OPEN SHAPE-2-INFINITY-Z3
   201	
   202	**Verdict. NECESSARY** as a successor on the `g=2`, `u≡3 (mod 6)` survivors. Claim (3.4) HOLDS for affine *nodes*; it is not checked for tangential `A_{2k-1}`.
   203	
   204	Shirane, hashed arXiv:1211.2526v1, Corollary 0.6 is literally `deg Δ̄=6`. Family 2 has branch `D̄` of degree `d=gu`, equal to 6 only at `(6,4)`. There is no promoted degree-`2k` analogue; for `deg B≥8` the double plane is of general type. The classification half of the `(6,4)` kill does not travel. CONFIRMED.
   205	
   206	The descent half *is* degree-free, and at `g=2` it is automatic: (3.3) puts `Π∈V_4`. It also forces `sgn Π=+1`, hence `d` even, hence (with `u` odd) `g` even: no odd-`g` family-2 row admits the `S_3` descent. Those rows are not killed; they lose the route.
